# GMS runs it over 20 levels at 141+8x with 2 attacks; here it is the same
# climb in half the steps, ending where GMS ends.
#
# The one attack in this book that is fire, and the only reason the tag
# exists: Ignite follows it and leaves Poison Breath alone.
#
# The cooldown is not a cost. It is barely half a swing, so the other half of
# the pair is always ready to fill it -- which is what makes the two alternate
# rather than the better one being cast forever. See fight.h.
name: "Flame Orb"
skill_order: 1
description:
  "Rolls a burning orb through the enemies in front of you. A fire spell, so "
  "Ignite follows it."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
tags: SKILL_TAG_FIRE
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_WIZARD
max_level: 10
base_delay_ms: 720
max_enemies: 6
lines: 2
cooldown_seconds: 0.5
base { skill_pct: 1.48 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.17 }
